From 4901f02a31148f858b4282a27d36c069157bd6fc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: anyingiit <49945850+anyingiit@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 19:14:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Respect serde(default) when setting minItems for tuple
 structs

When deserializing a tuple struct, serde fills in trailing elements that
are missing from the sequence using their default values, if the field or
the container has `#[serde(default)]`. The generated "deserialize" schema
previously always set `minItems` to the number of elements, so it rejected
input like `["abc"]` that deserializes successfully.

Now `minItems` (for the deserialize contract) only counts elements up to
the last one without a default. The serialize schema is unchanged.

Fixes #536
